  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nCurrently the WebDriver-BiDi spec `browser.close` [command](https://w3c.github.io/webdriver-bidi/#command-browser-close) - \r\nDefines step 4.3 - `Close any top-level browsing contexts without prompting to unload.`\r\nThis will be used also for another command - `browsingContext.close` when https://github.com/w3c/webdriver-bidi/pull/518 is merged. \r\n\r\nWe want to close a top-level browsing context without prompting any `beforeunload` handles.  \r\nIn the HTML spec there is no definition of how this has to be done and currently works by \"magic\".\r\n\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\n_No response_\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nA suggestion on how to implement this can be found on this comment https://github.com/w3c/webdriver-bidi/pull/518#issuecomment-1783113251 :\r\n\r\n```text\r\nIt seems like we could reuse the existing `WebDriver BiDi user prompt opened` steps \r\nby allowing them to return a value that specifies whether to show the prompt or not...\r\n```\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
